+{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"4430b698-12bb-49ba-86b9-f14b8afd9824","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_esyia4rBMZqRBeqClgSr8848","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/CONTRACT.md","content":"# DocumentStore Contract\n\n## 1. Document CRUD\n\n### 1.1 Create\n- [ ] `store.create(id, content)` stores a document with the given content on the current branch\n- [ ] `store.create(id, content)` deep-clones the content (mutating the original after create does not affect stored document)\n- [ ] `store.create(id, content)` throws if a document with the same ID already exists on the current branch\n- [ ] `store.create(id, content)` does NOT throw if the same ID exists on a different branch\n- [ ] Creating a document generates a version (see 2.1)\n\n### 1.2 Get\n- [ ] `store.get(id)` returns the current content of the document on the active branch\n- [ ] `store.get(id)` returns a deep clone (mutating the returned object does not affect stored document)\n- [ ] `store.get(id)` throws if the document doesn't exist on the current branch\n- [ ] `store.get(id)` throws if the document was deleted on the current branch\n\n### 1.3 Update\n- [ ] `store.update(id, content)` replaces the document content on the current branch\n- [ ] `store.update(id, content)` deep-clones the content\n- [ ] `store.update(id, content)` throws if the document doesn't exist on the current branch\n- [ ] `store.update(id, content)` throws if the document was deleted on the current branch\n- [ ] Updating a document generates a version (see 2.1)\n\n### 1.4 Delete\n- [ ] `store.delete(id)` removes the document on the current branch\n- [ ] After delete, `store.get(id)` throws on that branch\n- [ ] `store.delete(id)` throws if the document doesn't exist on the current branch\n- [ ] `store.delete(id)` throws if already deleted\n- [ ] Deleting does not affect other branches\n- [ ] Deleted documents are NOT visible on other branches (they still exist there)\n\n## 2. Version History\n\n### 2.1 Version Creation\n- [ ] Every `create` generates a version entry\n- [ ] Every `update` generates a version entry\n- [ ] `delete` does NOT generate a version entry\n- [ ] Each version has a unique `id` string (never reused across the store)\n- [ ] Each version has a `timestamp` number\n- [ ] Each version has the full document `content` at that point\n\n### 2.2 getHistory\n- [ ] `getHistory(id)` returns versions in chronological order (oldest first)\n- [ ] `getHistory(id)` returns versions only for the current branch\n- [ ] `getHistory(id)` throws if the document doesn't exist on the current branch\n- [ ] `getHistory(id)` throws if the document was deleted\n- [ ] The returned versions are deep-cloned\n\n### 2.3 getVersion\n- [ ] `getVersion(id, versionId)` returns the document content at that specific version\n- [ ] `getVersion(id, versionId)` throws if the version doesn't exist for that document\n- [ ] `getVersion(id, versionId)` throws if the document doesn't exist\n- [ ] Returns a deep clone\n\n## 3. Branching\n\n### 3.1 Default branch\n- [ ] The store starts on branch `\"main\"` by default\n- [ ] `store.getBranch()` returns `\"main\"` initially\n\n### 3.2 createBranch\n- [ ] `store.createBranch(name)` creates a new branch from the current branch's state\n- [ ] `store.createBranch(name, fromBranch)` creates from the specified branch\n- [ ] New branch starts with all documents from the source branch\n- [ ] Creating a branch does NOT switch to it\n- [ ] `createBranch` with a name that already exists throws\n\n### 3.3 switchBranch\n- [ ] `store.switchBranch(name)` changes the active branch\n- [ ] All subsequent CRUD operations apply to the switched branch\n- [ ] `switchBranch` to a non-existent branch throws\n\n### 3.4 Branch isolation\n- [ ] Changes on one branch are not visible on other branches\n- [ ] Documents created/modified/deleted on branch A do not affect branch B\n\n### 3.5 getBranch / listBranches\n- [ ] `store.getBranch()` returns the current branch name\n- [ ] `store.listBranches()` returns all branch names (including `\"main\"`)\n- [ ] `listBranches` returns a new array (not the internal reference)\n\n## 4. Three-Way Merge\n\n### 4.1 Common ancestor\n- [ ] Merge finds the common ancestor (fork point) of the two branches\n- [ ] The base for merge is the document state at the divergence point\n\n### 4.2 No conflicts — auto-applied\n- [ ] If only one side changed a field, take that change\n- [ ] If both sides changed same field to same value, no conflict\n- [ ] If one document changed on only one branch, take that change\n- [ ] When no conflicts, `applied` is `true`\n- [ ] When no conflicts, merge is applied to current branch\n- [ ] When no conflicts, `merged` contains the resulting documents\n- [ ] When no conflicts, conflicts array is empty\n\n### 4.3 With conflicts — not applied\n- [ ] When there are conflicts, `applied` is `false`\n- [ ] When there are conflicts, current branch is NOT modified\n- [ ] When there are conflicts, conflicts array contains the conflict details\n- [ ] Each conflict has `documentId`, `path`, `base`, `ours`, `theirs`\n- [ ] Path is dot-separated for nested fields (e.g., \"a.b.c\")\n- [ ] When there are conflicts, `merged` still shows what it would look like (ours wins in conflicts)\n\n### 4.4 No-op merge\n- [ ] Merging two branches with identical state produces no changes\n- [ ] `applied` is `true`, `merged` has current content, `conflicts` is empty\n\n### 4.5 Structural merge (nested objects)\n- [ ] Two branches modifying different nested keys of the same parent merge cleanly\n- [ ] Two branches modifying the same nested key to different values produce a conflict at that path\n- [ ] Arrays are treated as leaf values (compared by value equality, not merged element-wise)\n\n### 4.6 Multi-document merge\n- [ ] Changes to different documents on different branches merge cleanly with no conflicts\n\n### 4.7 Deletion during merge\n- [ ] If one side deletes a document and the other doesn't change it, deletion wins\n- [ ] If one side deletes and the other modifies, it's a conflict\n\n### 4.8 New documents on branches\n- [ ] A document created on one branch (not in base/other) is taken as-is\n- [ ] A document created independently on both branches with different content is a conflict\n\n### 4.9 Merging preserves versions on target\n- [ ] After a successful (applied) merge, a new version is created for each merged document on the current branch\n- [ ] After a successful merge, the merged content is retrievable via get()\n\n## 5. Edge Cases\n\n### 5.1 Empty document\n- [ ] Creating a document with `{}` works\n- [ ] Updating a document to `{}` works\n\n### 5.2 Deeply nested documents\n- [ ] Deeply nested objects (5+ levels) are handled correctly\n- [ ] Deep clone preserves all nesting\n\n### 5.3 Arrays\n- [ ] Documents can contain arrays as field values\n- [ ] Arrays are deep-cloned correctly\n- [ ] Arrays are treated as leaf values during merge (compared by value)\n\n### 5.4 Null values\n- [ ] Fields can have `null` values\n- [ ] `null` fields are deep-cloned correctly\n\n### 5.5 Multiple updates\n- [ ] Multiple updates create multiple versions\n- [ ] Each version preserves the content at that point in time\n\n### 5.6 Branch from non-default branch\n- [ ] createBranch with fromBranch parameter works correctly\n\n### 5.7 Fast-forward merge (one branch ahead of the other)\n- [ ] If source branch is ahead of target (target hasn't changed since fork), merge is fast-forward\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":55,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":27136,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94236fb2-ffb3-401b-aa1c-e9c2a4c9ed0b","uuid":"cb07d283-ce6f-45a0-9fa2-2c7d4012865d"}
